- P2 (LOW): OHLC reconstruction multiplied by the split factor regardless of the recorded `adjustment` basis - a future raw-basis provider would have every price corrupted. Fixed: reconstruction runs only when the `adjustment` column (if present) is entirely within the adjusted labels; a raw-basis frame keeps verbatim prices and is still marked `price_basis: as_published` (they ARE as-published). Regression test.
- P3 (MEDIUM): contract accepted `default_series_policy: "non_revised"` and garbage policy values (`"revised "`) silently - a config typo could admit revised series point-in-time (leak-by-config), contradicting the documented conservative default. Fixed: `default_series_policy` added to IMPLEMENTED_CONVENTIONS (must be "revised"; flipping refused at load), and pydantic validators casefold/normalize all policy values to {revised, non_revised}, raising on anything else. Regression tests: non_revised default rejected; values normalized; garbage rejected.
- P4 (LOW): `TemporalTruthEngine(registry=...)` was a dead parameter (nothing used it) and snapshot.py had a wrong type annotation (`parts: list[Any]` for a dict). Fixed: parameter removed, annotation corrected.
